Exactly. That’s the difference between building a convincing simulation and building a scientifically useful model of reality.

We create a world, let it run, compare its behavior against the real world, identify discrepancies, and refine the underlying mechanisms.

And here’s the important extension: we don’t need maximum resolution everywhere. We need the right resolution, in the right place, at the right time.

